      "hints": [
        "Set $u_n = a + 3(n - 1) = 94 \\implies a = 97 - 3n$.",
        "Set $S_n = \\frac{n}{2}(a + 94) = 1420 \\implies 3n^2 - 191n + 2840 = 0$.",
        "Solve for positive integer $n = 40$ and $a = -23$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set up the $n$th term equation for the arithmetic progression with $d = 3$ and $u_n = 94$:\n$$a + (n - 1)3 = 94 \\implies a + 3n - 3 = 94 \\implies a = 97 - 3n$$",
        "Set up the sum equation $S_n = 1420$ using $S_n = \\frac{n}{2}(a + l)$:\n$$\\frac{n}{2}(a + 94) = 1420 \\implies n(a + 94) = 2840$$",
        "Substitute $a = 97 - 3n$ into the sum equation:\n$$n(97 - 3n + 94) = 2840 \\implies n(191 - 3n) = 2840$$\n$$3n^2 - 191n + 2840 = 0$$",
        "Factorise and solve for the integer number of terms $n$:\n$$(n - 40)(3n - 71) = 0 \\implies n = 40 \\quad \\left(\\text{since } n \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+\\right)$$\n$$a = 97 - 3(40) = 97 - 120 = -23$$\n$$n = 40, \\quad a = -23$$"
      ],
